<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Raumarike</h1><p class="st-meta">750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Petty kingdom of the Romerike plain north-east of Oslo, site of the Eidsivating assembly and an early conquest of Halfdan the Black.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Raumarike covered the broad farming lowland of Romerike, north-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslofjord">Oslofjord</a>. It is known only from the sagas, which describe it as a small kingdom taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halfdan-the-black">Halfdan the Black of Vestfold</a> in the 9th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The district was among the most fertile in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, with dense settlement along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glomma">Glomma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vorma">Vorma</a> rivers. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eidsivating">Eidsivating</a>, the law assembly of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upplands-norway">Upplands</a>, met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eidsvoll">Eidsvoll</a> in the region, giving it a role in the legal life of inland Norway.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halfdan-the-black">Halfdan the Black</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> incorporated Raumarike into their growing realm, and it became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eidsvoll">Eidsvoll</a> later gained national fame as the place where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway's</a> constitution was adopted in 1814.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/raumarike.jpg" alt="Raumarike" width="320" height="423"><figcaption>Image: Worldlydev · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nedre_og_%C3%98vre_Romerike.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>750 CE – 880 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Norway</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Romerike, Kingdom of Raumarike</dd></dl></aside></div>
